	-> EBS : virtual storage provided to yr instance
		- It will keep data safe even after deleting instance, we can attach this volume to another instance and after that by resizing file system and mounting any partition to previously mounted directory we can get that data
		
	-> we can only increase the size of volume by modify volume, can't decrease
		- after resizing volume we need to resize file system also : first e2fsck -f /dev/sda1, then resize2fs /dev/sda1
		- to resize xfs file system : xfs_growfs
	
	-> resize root EBS volume : after resizing by modify volume...
		- first we have to extend the part of that block by growpart /dev/sda 1(1st part of /dev/sda)
		- after that resize the file system
		
	-> attach one EBS volume to multiple instance(volume type io2 necessary)
		- we can attach only instances that are the part of "Nitro(latest architecture)" and not "Xen(older architecture)" instances.
		
		
		
		
	
